
1. Install XRDP

sudo apt update
sudo apt install xrdp -y

2. Start and Enable XRDP Service

sudo systemctl start xrdp
sudo systemctl enable xrdp

3. Install XFCE Desktop Environment

sudo apt install xfce4 xfce4-goodies dbus-x11 xorgxrdp -y

4. Configure XRDP to Use XFCE
Edit the startwm.sh script:


sudo vim /etc/xrdp/startwm.sh
#Replace the content with:

#!/bin/sh
unset DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
unset XDG_RUNTIME_DIR

startxfce4

sudo chmod +x /etc/xrdp/startwm.sh

5. Set User Session to XFCE

echo "startxfce4" > ~/.xsession
chmod +x ~/.xsession

6. Restart XRDP Service
sudo systemctl restart xrdp
